---
title: Fresh Gooseberry Cake
source: Mum
author: Edna Faith Thoukydides
course: Dessert
locale: en_GB
prep time: 30m
cook time: 1h
difficulty: Medium
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- vegetarian
- cake
- sweet
- dessert
---

= Cake Base =

Top and tail the @green gooseberries{450%g}. Wash and pat dry.

Cream the @butter{110%g} and @caster sugar{110%g}. Lightly beat the @eggs{2} with the @vanilla essence{0.5%tsp}, and beat into the creamed mixture a little at a time. Add a little of the @self-raising flour{170%g}(sifted) along with the last few additions of egg. Using a metal spoon gently fold in the remaining flour, @salt{pinch}, and sufficient @milk to make a medium soft consistency.

Grease a #9 inch round tin (with loose base or clipped sides){}. Spread the mixture evenly over the base of the tin. Cover with the prepared gooseberries.

= Topping =

To make the topping mix the @self-raising flour{110%g} and @caster sugar{85%g}, then rub in the @butter{85%g}. Use a fork to stir in @water{1%tbsp} until the mixture clings together in larger lumps.

Sprinkle the crumble topping over the gooseberries to cover them.

= Bake =

Preheat the oven to 180°C (160°C fan). Bake for ~{1%hour} in the centre of the oven.

Bake from cold on shelf level 2 using the "Cakes in deep tins" baking sensor programme.

Allow the cake to cool before removing from the tin. Sprinkle the surface with @icing sugar{}.